Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] scsi: ufs: qcom: run HS-G5 at the 300 MHz OPP on HW ver 5

With an OPP table, ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed() derives the gear from the
UniPro clock of the target OPP: 403 MHz gives HS-G5 and 300 MHz HS-G4.
SM8550 (UFS controller HW ver 5) has no 403 MHz UniPro rate; its top OPP is
300 MHz, so every scale-up put the link at HS-G4 although the controller
(PARAM0), the PHY (G5 tables, already used at power-up) and a UFS 4.0
device all support HS-G5.  The HW ver 5 rule that pins Rate-A whenever the
PHY is set up for G5 then left the link at G4 Rate-A, below even G4 Rate-B.

Qualcomm's Kalama driver, as shipped by Samsung on these tablets, runs
HS-G5 Rate-A with the UniPro clock at 300 MHz.  Map 300 MHz to G5 on HW
ver 5; the existing clamp to the negotiated maximum keeps UFS 3.1 devices
at G4.  Measured before: HS_GEAR4 / HS_RATE_A under load on the SM-X710.
Not yet validated on hardware.

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2490,6 +2490,7 @@
 
 static u32 ufs_qcom_freq_to_gear_speed(struct ufs_hba *hba, unsigned long freq)
 {
+	struct ufs_qcom_host *host = ufshcd_get_variant(hba);
 	u32 gear = UFS_HS_DONT_CHANGE;
 	unsigned long unipro_freq;
 
@@ -2502,7 +2503,11 @@
 		gear = UFS_HS_G5;
 		break;
 	case 300000000:
-		gear = UFS_HS_G4;
+		/*
+		 * HW ver 5 (SM8550) has no 403 MHz UniPro clock: it runs HS-G5
+		 * Rate-A at 300 MHz, as the Kalama downstream driver does.
+		 */
+		gear = host->hw_ver.major == 0x5 ? UFS_HS_G5 : UFS_HS_G4;
 		break;
 	case 201500000:
 		gear = UFS_HS_G3;
